## Notes

- **Enforced FK relationships:** `ATTENDANCE.userId â†’ USER.id` (ON DELETE CASCADE); `USER.managerId â†’
  USER.id` self-reference (Tenant âŸ¶ Staff); `CAMERA.zone_id â†’ MONITORINGZONE.id`;
  `DETECTIONALERT.camera_id â†’ CAMERA.id` and `DETECTIONALERT.zone_id â†’ MONITORINGZONE.id` (both
  nullable â€” the AI engine's string payload still works); `SUPPORTTICKET.transcriptId â†’
  CHATTRANSCRIPT.id` (ChatTranscript `hasOne` SupportTicket).
- **Soft links (no DB-level FK, matched at query time):**
  - `BOOKING.tenantId â†’ USER.id` â€” Staff bookings use the Staff member's `managerId`.
  - `SECURITYLOG.personnelName â†’ USER.name` â€” nulled on PDPA off-boarding.
  - `MONITORINGZONE.assigned_team` â€” free-text response-team name, not an FK.
  - `DETECTIONALERT â†’ INCIDENTLOG` â€” object-detection alerts can seed incident records (soft workflow).
- **KNOWLEDGEBASE** is standalone FAQ data used by the AI Helpdesk to match incoming chat messages.
- `faceVector` is a PostgreSQL `FLOAT[]` array (Sequelize `ARRAY(FLOAT)`) â€” **not pgvector**
  (pgvector not required).
- Soft-deletable (`paranoid`) tables keep a `deletedAt` timestamp: bookings, cameras, monitoring
  zones, detection alerts, incident logs.
